{"seconds": 53.9, "exit": 0, "final": "If Kf8, then Qxg7+ wins the queen. The bottom line is: **Rh8+ is the key move**\u2014it sacrifices the rook to expose Black's king to a decisive attack. After 1...Kxh8 2.Qh6+ Kg8, White has multiple winning continuations (3.Qh8+ or 3.Qh7+), and if 1...Qxh8 2.Qg8+ wins material immediately.\n\n**Coaching Note:** This is a back-rank sacrifice motif. When the opponent's king is exposed on the h-file with limited escape squares, a rook sacrifice that brings your queen into the attack with tempo can be devastating. Look for this when: (1) the king is trapped on the edge, (2) you have queen + rook control nearby, (3) enemy pieces are blocked from defending. After Rh8+, Black is forced into a losing position\u2014either the king gets mated or the queen is captured.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rh8+\", \"line\": [\"Rh8+\", \"Kxh8\", \"Qh6+\", \"Kg8\", \"Qh7+\", \"Kf8\"], \"motifs\": [\"backRankMate\", \"sacrifice\", \"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1bR4/ppp1rpqk/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 w - - 6 22"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1bR4/ppp1rpqk/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 w - - 6 22"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1bR4/ppp1rpqk/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 w - - 6 22"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1bR4/ppp1rpqk/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 w - - 6 22", "move": "Rh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b4R/ppp1rpqk/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 b - - 7 22", "move": "Kxh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b4R/ppp1rpqk/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 b - - 7 22", "move": "Qxh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b4k/ppp1rpq1/2n5/4p1Q1/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 w - - 0 23", "move": "Qh6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b4k/ppp1rpq1/2n4Q/4p3/8/2P3PP/PP3P2/4R1K1 b - - 1 23", "move":